      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and remember: I joined a woodworking workshop last weekend with my colleague, Tom. We learned how to craft intricate wooden furniture pieces from scratch and I made a beautiful oak coffee table. Tom and I are planning to work on a custom bookshelf together next.",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ve saved this memory.\n\nSummary saved: You attended a woodworking workshop last weekend with your colleague Tom, learned to craft intricate wooden furniture, made a beautiful oak coffee table, and you and Tom are planning to build a custom bookshelf next.\n\nWould you like me to do any of the following now?\n- Draft/send a message to Tom (examples below).\n- Create a short social post caption.\n- Save it as a dated journal entry or note (add trip dates if you want).\n- Create a calendar reminder or task for the bookshelf project (with a preferred start date).\n- Add/organize photos or tag this memory for easy lookup later.\n- Nothing else — just keep it in my notes.\n\nExample messages you can pick or edit:\n- To Tom (casual): “Hey Tom — I had a great time at the woodworking workshop. Loved making the oak coffee table — excited to start the custom bookshelf with you. When shall we plan the first session?”\n- To Tom (short): “Loved the workshop — let’s schedule time to start the bookshelf project!”\n- Social caption: “Made an oak coffee table at a woodworking workshop with Tom — next up: a custom bookshelf. #woodworking #DIY”\n\nWhich would you like me to do?",
      "duration_s": 8.717,
